<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides a brief overview of some formulations and assumptions from the high-rate quantization literature. This should help to compare the formulations between the standard quantization problem and our MoE learning problem. For more details see the overview by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray and Neuhoff (1998)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Approximated Error Formula</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider scalar quantization for a random input <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from the probability distribution function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The quantizer design requires to segment the input space <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> intervals <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{[a_{i-1},a_{i})\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{[a_{i-1},a_{i})\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=a_{0}&lt;a_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;a_{m-1}&lt;a_{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=a_{0}&lt;a_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;a_{m-1}&lt;a_{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math>; formally, the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\sf th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝗍𝗁</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\sf th}</annotation></semantics></math> interval is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a_{m-1},a_{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a_{m-1},a_{m}]</annotation></semantics></math> but for writing simplicity it will be written as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a_{m-1},a_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a_{m-1},a_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> as the other intervals. Each interval has a unique representation value: <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i},~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i},~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The quantizer function can be written as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)=v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)=v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[a_{i-1},a_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[a_{i-1},a_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The performance criterion is the expected squared error</p>
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{Q}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathrm{x}}\left[{{\left(Q(\mathrm{x})-\mathrm{x}\right)^{2}}}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(v_{i}-x\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{Q}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathrm{x}}\left[{{\left(Q(\mathrm{x})-\mathrm{x}\right)^{2}}}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(v_{i}-x\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under the high-rate quantization assumption, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is large such that the intervals are sufficiently small and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is approximately constant within each of them, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\approx p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})~~\text{for}~x\in[a_{i-1},a_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\approx p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})~~\text{for}~x\in[a_{i-1},a_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\triangleq\frac{a_{i-1}+a_{i}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\triangleq\frac{a_{i-1}+a_{i}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the center of the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\rm th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>th</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\rm th}</annotation></semantics></math> interval. This implies that, for a given segmentation, the optimal representation values are the interval centers, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=x_{i},~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=x_{i},~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Based on these, the high-rate quantization literature uses the approximated error formula:</p>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{Q}\approx\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\int\displaylimits_{x=0}^{1}{\frac{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}{g^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{Q}\approx\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\int\displaylimits_{x=0}^{1}{\frac{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}{g^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where the smooth function <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> has the following meanings:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the compander design that turns a uniform quantizer (whose intervals have equal length) into a nonuniform one <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bennett, 1948</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Panter and Dite, 1951</a>)</cite>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is the derivative of a nonlinear function which is applied as a preprocessing and its inverse as postprocessing to a uniform quantizer. Namely, if <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm unif}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>unif</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm unif}</annotation></semantics></math> is a uniform quantizer over <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> whose quantization interval length is <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, a nonuniform quantizer can be formed by <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)=v\left(Q_{\rm unif}(u(x))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>unif</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)=v\left(Q_{\rm unif}(u(x))\right)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is a preprocessing function (called compressor) and its inverse is the postprocessing function <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> (called expander). In (<a href="#A1.E45" title="In A.1 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Approximated Error Formula ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) we have <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=u^{\prime}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=u^{\prime}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For nonuniform quantizers in general (i.e., also beyond the compander design), <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lloyd (1982)</a></cite> defined <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> as the density of quantization intervals.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">It was importantly shown by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Panter and Dite (1951)</a></cite> that the quantization error (<a href="#A1.E45" title="In A.1 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Approximated Error Formula ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) is minimized by</p>
<table id="A1.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\rm opt}(x)=\frac{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mroot><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mroot><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\rm opt}(x)=\frac{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">which attains the minimal quantization error of</p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{Q}^{\sf opt}\approx\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\left({\int\displaylimits_{x=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}}\right)^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></munderover><mroot><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{Q}^{\sf opt}\approx\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\left({\int\displaylimits_{x=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\mathrm{d}x}}}\right)^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the compander design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bennett, 1948</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Panter and Dite, 1951</a>)</cite>, the optimal compressor function is obtained by integrating <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\rm opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\rm opt}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A1.E46" title="In A.1 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Approximated Error Formula ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x)=\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{x}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{x}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi}{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{1}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x)=\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{x}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{x}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi}{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{1}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The compander design requires also an expander function <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the inverse of the compressor <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A1.E48" title="In A.2 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{v(x)}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi=x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{v(x)}g^{\rm opt}(\xi)\mathrm{d}\xi=x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The equation (<a href="#A1.E49" title="In A.2 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) has a unique solution when <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\rm opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>opt</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\rm opt}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive over <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, here this requires that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is positive over <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>; this will make the compressor function strictly monotonic increasing and therefore invertible.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">More generally than the compander design, the optimal quantization intervals (i.e., optimal segmentation of the input space <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>) are defined by the optimal expander from (<a href="#A1.E49" title="In A.2 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\rm opt}=v\left(\frac{i}{m}\right),~~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>opt</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\rm opt}=v\left(\frac{i}{m}\right),~~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Importantly, for the multidimensional case of vector quantizers, it is generally impossible to form the optimal segmentation by extending (<a href="#A1.E48" title="In A.2 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>)-(<a href="#A1.E50" title="In A.2 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>); this is because multidimensional quantization regions are defined by their shapes and not just by their volumes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">More explanations about the multidimensional case of vector quantizers are provided throughout our multidimensional MoE learning analysis in Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>; for more details see Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 High-Rate Quantization Theory ‣ 2 Relate Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> and the detailed overview by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray and Neuhoff (1998)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Related Work: Gersho’s Conjecture for High-Rate Vector Quantization</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gersho’s conjecture is true when the <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional space can be optimally tesselated by a lattice, i.e., by one optimal polytope; this is known to hold for <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math> by intervals, for <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math> by hexagons <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fejes Toth, 1959</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Newman, 1982</a>)</cite>. For <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=3</annotation></semantics></math>, it is informally believed that the optimal tessellation is the body-centered cubic lattice, which was proved as the optimal lattice tesselation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Barnes and Sloane, 1983</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du and Wang, 2005</a>)</cite>.
For <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, it is unknown if the optimal tessellation is by lattice and if Gersho’s conjecture is accurate. Yet, as explained by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray and Neuhoff (1998)</a></cite>, considering the relation between the conjecture to an unspecified constant from the rigorous theory by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zador (1982)</a></cite>, the conjecture inaccuracy for <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> is not expected to significantly affect the approximated error; moreover, a theoretical result by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zamir and Feder (1996)</a></cite> implies that the conjecture inaccuracy vanishes as <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. A detailed discussion on the conjecture is given by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray and Neuhoff (1998)</a></cite>.
All of these established Gersho’s conjecture as a useful tool for high-rate vector quantization theory; in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> we use this conjecture to theoretically analyze the segmentation that minimizes the test error upper bound of mixture of many experts for multidimensional inputs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To proceed from the point where Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> ends, we use a widely-believed conjecture for high-rate vector quantization by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gersho (1979)</a></cite>; see Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 High-Rate Quantization Theory ‣ 2 Relate Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Related Work: Gersho’s Conjecture for High-Rate Vector Quantization ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray and Neuhoff, 1998</a>)</cite> for more details.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5</span></span><span id="Thmassumption5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The large number of experts and the small region assumption induce regions whose shapes are approximately congruent to the optimal convex polytope <math id="Thmassumption5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{{\sf opt},d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{{\sf opt},d}</annotation></semantics></math> that tesselates the <math id="Thmassumption5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional space. Accordingly,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\boldsymbol{x})\approx M(A_{{\sf opt},d})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\boldsymbol{x})\approx M(A_{{\sf opt},d})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="Thmassumption5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, this assumption leads to the following test error bound for the multidimensional MoE.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, the approximation of the upper bound from (<a href="#S5.E30" title="In Corollary 5. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="A3.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d\cdot M(A_{{\sf opt},d})}{m^{2/d}}\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\frac{\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mi>𝖻𝗈𝗎𝗇𝖽</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d\cdot M(A_{{\sf opt},d})}{m^{2/d}}\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\frac{\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, the following theorem provides the upper-bound minimizing (UBM) expert segment density function <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\sf UBM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝖴𝖡𝖬</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\sf UBM}</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding error bound.
Note that (<a href="#A3.E52" title="In Corollary 12. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) is an upper bound for the approximation error <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\sf app}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗉</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\sf app}</annotation></semantics></math> of the hypothesis class <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{m,d}^{c}\left(\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{m,d}^{c}\left(\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The test error’s upper bound <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mi>𝖻𝗈𝗎𝗇𝖽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.E52" title="In Corollary 12. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) is minimized by the expert segment density function</span></p>
<table id="A3.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\sf UBM}(\boldsymbol{x})=\frac{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{\xi}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{\xi})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{\xi})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}\right)}^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{\xi}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝖴𝖡𝖬</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝝃</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝝃</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\sf UBM}(\boldsymbol{x})=\frac{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{\xi}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{\xi})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{\xi})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}\right)}^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{\xi}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">that attains the minimal upper bound of the test error:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound,min}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d\cdot M(A_{d}^{\sf opt})}{m^{2/d}}\left({\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}\right)}^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{1+\frac{2}{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mrow><mi>𝖻𝗈𝗎𝗇𝖽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound,min}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d\cdot M(A_{d}^{\sf opt})}{m^{2/d}}\left({\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}}\right)}^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{1+\frac{2}{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The theorem proof is provided in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error in the Multidimensional Case ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The segment density in (<a href="#A3.E53" title="In Theorem 13. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) minimizes the upper bound of the test error, and does not directly minimize the test error. Optimizing an objective’s bound is a valid heuristic approach for when the objective optimization is intractable (e.g., as commonly done for variational autoencoders <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Welling, 2014</a>)</cite>); the assumption is that minimization of the objective’s upper bound would promote minimization of the true objective. However, usually the upper-bound minimizing solution does not achieve the minimum of the true objective. An important aspect of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem 13. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> is the connection to the corresponding results for high-rate vector quantization by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gersho (1979)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Na and Neuhoff (1995)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Regardless to the suboptimality due to minimizing an upper bound, there is an important difference between the multidimensional and one-dimensional cases. in the one-dimensional case, it is possible to form an optimal segmentation from the optimal segment density function (whose values are positive over the entire input domain, see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Scalar High-Rate Quantization: Forming a Quantizer from a Quantization Segment Density ‣ Appendix A High Rate Quantization: Formulations from Related Work ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>); but in the multidimensional case, it is usually impossible to form an optimal segmentation from the optimal segment density function due to the ambiguity in the optimal shapes of the segmentation regions. More detailed discussions on this appear in the high-rate vector quantization literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gersho, 1979</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Na and Neuhoff, 1995</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray and Neuhoff, 1998</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs for Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of the Test Error Formula for Multidimensional MoE in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following proof is based on the data model (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and the MoE predictor form (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathrm{y}}\left[{{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\mathrm{y}\right)^{2}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathrm{y}}\left[{{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\mathrm{y}\right)^{2}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\epsilon}\left[{{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\beta(\mathbf{x})-{\epsilon}\right)^{2}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\epsilon}\left[{{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\beta(\mathbf{x})-{\epsilon}\right)^{2}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\left[{{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\beta(\mathbf{x})\right)^{2}}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}\left[{{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\beta(\mathbf{x})\right)^{2}}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\beta(\mathbf{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\left(\widehat{\beta}(\mathbf{x})-\beta(\mathbf{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of the Optimal Constants in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given segmentation <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal constants <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined by the minimization problem:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}}{\argmin}\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">m</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}}{\argmin}\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}}{\argmin}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">m</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}}{\argmin}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is a convex minimization problem; hence, the optimal constants satisfy</p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial c_{i}}\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=0,~~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial c_{i}}\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=0,~~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Our test error formula (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) implies that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial c_{i}}\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{2\left(c_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial c_{i}}\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{2\left(c_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and, therefore, (<a href="#A4.E58" title="In D.2 Proof of the Optimal Constants in Eq. () ‣ Appendix D Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) implies</p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}},~~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}},~~\forall i\in\{1,\dots,m\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which proves (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>: The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a start, note that the first-order Taylor approximation of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E17" title="In 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) imply the approximation of their product as</p>
<table id="A5.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(x)p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)=\beta(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\beta(x_{i})\right)\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(x)p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)=\beta(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\beta(x_{i})\right)\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, setting the approximations (<a href="#S4.E17" title="In 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), (<a href="#A5.E61" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) into (<a href="#S4.E15" title="In 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left({\beta(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\beta(x_{i})\right)\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left({\beta(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\beta(x_{i})\right)\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\beta(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}+o\left(\Delta_{i}^{2}\right)}{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}+o\left(\Delta_{i}^{2}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\beta(x_{i})p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}+o\left(\Delta_{i}^{2}\right)}{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}+o\left(\Delta_{i}^{2}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the following basic results were used:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}\mathrm{d}x=\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}\mathrm{d}x=\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}(x-x_{i})\mathrm{d}x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}(x-x_{i})\mathrm{d}x=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x\in o\left(\Delta_{i}^{2}\right)~~\text{as}~\Delta_{i}\rightarrow 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>as</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x\in o\left(\Delta_{i}^{2}\right)~~\text{as}~\Delta_{i}\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The proof of (<a href="#A5.E65" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) is based on the little-o definition: <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)\in o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)\in o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\rightarrow x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\rightarrow x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underset{x\rightarrow x_{i}}{\lim}\frac{f(x)}{\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underset{x\rightarrow x_{i}}{\lim}\frac{f(x)}{\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and that for every <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert{\frac{f(x)}{\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert}}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert{\frac{f(x)}{\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert}}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert{f(x)}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert{f(x)}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>.
For an interval length <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i-1}=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i-1}=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then our integration over <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[a_{i-1},a_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[a_{i-1},a_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and the requirement <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> imply that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x}\right\rvert\leq\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}\left\lvert{o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)}\right\rvert\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x}\right\rvert\leq\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}\left\lvert{o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)}\right\rvert\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}\varepsilon\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\mathrm{d}x=2\varepsilon\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}(x-x_{i})\mathrm{d}x=\varepsilon\frac{\Delta_{i}^{2}}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}-\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}\varepsilon\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\mathrm{d}x=2\varepsilon\int\displaylimits_{x=x_{i}}^{x_{i}+\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}}(x-x_{i})\mathrm{d}x=\varepsilon\frac{\Delta_{i}^{2}}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">that implies</p>
<table id="A5.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x}\right\rvert}{\Delta_{i}^{2}}&lt;\frac{\varepsilon}{4}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert\right)\mathrm{d}x}\right\rvert}{\Delta_{i}^{2}}&lt;\frac{\varepsilon}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which holds for every <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and its existing <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that were defined above. Recall that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta_{i}}{2}\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, we get (<a href="#A5.E65" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We return to (<a href="#A5.Ex6" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>) to further develop it:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}\left({\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}\right)}{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}\left({1+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}\right)}=\frac{\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}{1+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}\left({\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}\right)}{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}\left({1+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}\right)}=\frac{\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}{1+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)\right)\left({\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)\right)\left({\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where (<a href="#A5.E69" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) is due to the little-o property: if <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)\in o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)\in o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1+o\left(f(x)\right)}=1+o\left(f(x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1+o\left(f(x)\right)}=1+o\left(f(x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By this, we complete the proof of (<a href="#S4.E18" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of the error formula (<a href="#S4.E19" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is by setting the linear approximations (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)-(<a href="#S4.E17" title="In 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) and the optimal constants for small subintervals (<a href="#S4.E18" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) in the error formula (<a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{a_{i}\}_{i=0}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{a_{i}\}_{i=0}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}\left(\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)-\left({\beta(x_{i})+\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(x)}\right)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}\left(\beta(x_{i})+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)-\left({\beta(x_{i})+\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(x)}\right)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathrm{x}},1}(x)}\right)\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="8.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathrm{x}},1}(x)}\right)\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~~~~\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(x)+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathrm{x}},1}(x)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~~~~\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(x)+o\left(\Delta_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathrm{x}},1}(x)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(x-x_{i}\right)^{2}\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(x-x_{i}\right)^{2}\left({p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})+p_{\mathrm{x}}^{\prime}(x_{i})\cdot\left(x-x_{i}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}x}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(x-x_{i}\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}x}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}{\left(x-x_{i}\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}x}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\cdot\frac{\Delta_{i}^{3}}{12}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)+\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\cdot\frac{\Delta_{i}^{3}}{12}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\cdot\frac{\Delta_{i}^{3}}{12}}\right)+o\left({\Delta_{\sf max}^{3}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({\left(\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\cdot\frac{\Delta_{i}^{3}}{12}}\right)+o\left({\Delta_{\sf max}^{3}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\sf max}=\underset{i\in\{1,\dots,m\}}{\max}\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\sf max}=\underset{i\in\{1,\dots,m\}}{\max}\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest subinterval. The developments in (<a href="#A5.E71" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) use (<a href="#A5.E64" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>) as well as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}(x-x_{i})^{3}\mathrm{d}x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}(x-x_{i})^{3}\mathrm{d}x=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert^{2}\right)\mathrm{d}x\in o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)~~\text{as}~\Delta_{i}\rightarrow 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>as</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{x=a_{i-1}}^{a_{i}}o\left(\lvert{x-x_{i}}\rvert^{2}\right)\mathrm{d}x\in o\left(\Delta_{i}^{3}\right)~~\text{as}~\Delta_{i}\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where (<a href="#A5.E73" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) can be proved similarly to (<a href="#A5.E65" title="In E.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>).
By this we conclude the proof of the test error formula (<a href="#S4.E19" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Additional Details on Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 2. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from the test error formula (<a href="#S4.E19" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Small Subintervals Assumption and Locally-Linear Approximations ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), we omit the explicit inaccuracy term <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left({\Delta_{\sf max}^{3}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left({\Delta_{\sf max}^{3}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and develop as follows:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\Delta_{i}^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\frac{1}{m^{2}\lambda^{2}\left(x_{i}\right)}\Delta_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12}\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x_{i})}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x_{i})\frac{1}{m^{2}\lambda^{2}\left(x_{i}\right)}\Delta_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\int_{x=0}^{1}{\frac{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\int_{x=0}^{1}{\frac{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The developments in (<a href="#A5.E74" title="In E.2 Additional Details on Corollary ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>) use Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and approximation of the sum as integral due to the small segment assumption.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>: The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us develop a lower bound for the integral <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{x=0}^{1}{\frac{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{x=0}^{1}{\frac{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}</annotation></semantics></math> from the test error formula of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 2. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. By Hölder’s inequality,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/3}(x)}}\right)^{3}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{1/3}\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\lambda^{2/3}(x)}\right)^{3/2}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{2/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mroot><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/3}(x)}}\right)^{3}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{1/3}\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\lambda^{2/3}(x)}\right)^{3/2}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{2/3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\geq\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="18.278em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mroot><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\geq\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the left side can be simplified, thus,</p>
<table id="A5.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{1/3}\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\lambda(x)\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{2/3}\geq\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mroot><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{1/3}\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\lambda(x)\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{2/3}\geq\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The density <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(x)</annotation></semantics></math> integrates to 1, i.e., <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{x=0}^{1}\lambda(x)\mathrm{d}x=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{x=0}^{1}\lambda(x)\mathrm{d}x=1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence, we get that</p>
<table id="A5.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x\geq\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mroot><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{x=0}^{1}\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}\mathrm{d}x\geq\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the left side is the integral from the test error formula of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 2. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Hölder’s inequality in (<a href="#A5.E75" title="In E.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>) is attained with equality if <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is linearly proportional to<math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Namely, for a constant <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda(x)=\zeta\cdot\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda(x)=\zeta\cdot\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which, using integration over <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and that the density integrates to 1, implies that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta=\frac{1}{\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mroot><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta=\frac{1}{\left({\int_{x=0}^{1}\sqrt[3]{\left({\beta^{\prime}(x)}\right)^{2}p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)}\mathrm{d}x}\right)^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the density that minimizes the integral in the left side of (<a href="#A5.E77" title="In E.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) is</p>
<table id="A5.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\sf opt}(x)=\frac{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\left(\beta^{\prime}(x)\right)^{2}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(\xi)\left(\beta^{\prime}(\xi)\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}\xi}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mroot><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mroot><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\sf opt}(x)=\frac{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\left(\beta^{\prime}(x)\right)^{2}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\xi=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(\xi)\left(\beta^{\prime}(\xi)\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}\xi}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The optimal density <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\sf opt}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\sf opt}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> makes (<a href="#A5.E77" title="In E.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) to hold with equality. Then, plugging the right side of (<a href="#A5.E77" title="In E.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error ‣ Appendix E Proofs for the Case of One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) into the the test error formula of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 2. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> gives the minimal test error of</p>
<table id="A5.E81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf opt}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\left({\int\displaylimits_{x=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\left(\beta^{\prime}(x)\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}x}}}\right)^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></munderover><mroot><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf opt}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{1}{12m^{2}}\left({\int\displaylimits_{x=0}^{1}{\sqrt[3]{p_{\mathrm{x}}(x)\left(\beta^{\prime}(x)\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}x}}}\right)^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4.2 Optimizing the Routing Segmentation using Expert Segment Density ‣ 4 Approximation Error of MoE for One-Dimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>: The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a start, note that the first-order Taylor approximation of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S5.E25" title="In 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) imply the approximation of their product as</p>
<table id="A6.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})=\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})=\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, setting the approximations (<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>), (<a href="#A6.E82" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>) into (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A6.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\nabla\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}\right)}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}\right)}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the following basic results were used:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=V(A_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=V(A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}\in o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}\right)~~\text{as}~V(A_{i})\rightarrow 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>as</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}\in o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}\right)~~\text{as}~V(A_{i})\rightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The proof of (<a href="#A6.E86" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>) is based on the little-o definition: <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\boldsymbol{x})\in o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\boldsymbol{x})\in o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}{\lim}\frac{f(\boldsymbol{x})}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}{\lim}\frac{f(\boldsymbol{x})}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and that for every <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert{\frac{f(\boldsymbol{x})}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}}}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert{\frac{f(\boldsymbol{x})}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}}}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert{f(\boldsymbol{x})}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert{f(\boldsymbol{x})}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the center of the region <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and that we are interested in integration over <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Accordingly,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\lvert{o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right\rvert\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\lvert{o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right\rvert\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\varepsilon\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\varepsilon\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Using the definition of the normalized <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\sf th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>𝗍𝗁</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\sf th}</annotation></semantics></math> moment of inertia,</p>
<table id="A6.E88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}(A_{i})\triangleq\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{k}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}{d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{k}{d}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}(A_{i})\triangleq\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{k}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}{d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{k}{d}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> and set it in (<a href="#A6.Ex21" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>) to yield</p>
<table id="A6.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right\rvert&lt;\varepsilon M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">i.e.,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right\rvert}{V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}}&lt;\varepsilon M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\left\lvert{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right\rvert}{V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}}&lt;\varepsilon M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">which holds for every <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and its existing <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> that were defined above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that using <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert{o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right\rvert&lt;\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert{o\left(\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\right)}\right\rvert&lt;\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A6.Ex21" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>) requires that <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\in(0,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\in(0,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., over the entire integrated region). This implies, using (<a href="#A6.E88" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">88</span></a>) for <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{1}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{1}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\delta\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=\frac{1}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}V(A_{i})\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{1}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\delta\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=\frac{1}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}V(A_{i})\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A6.E92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(A_{i})&lt;\left(\frac{\delta}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}\right)^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(A_{i})&lt;\left(\frac{\delta}{M_{1}(A_{i})\cdot d}\right)^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, (<a href="#A6.E90" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">90</span></a>) proves (<a href="#A6.E86" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let us return to (<a href="#A6.Ex20" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>) to further develop it,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}\right)}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})\left(1+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\right)}=\frac{\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}{1+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}\right)}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})V(A_{i})\left(1+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\right)}=\frac{\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}{1+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\right)\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\right)\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where (<a href="#A6.E94" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">94</span></a>) is due to the little-o property: if <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\boldsymbol{x})\in o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\boldsymbol{x})\in o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1+o\left(f(\boldsymbol{x})\right)}=1+o\left(f(\boldsymbol{x})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1+o\left(f(\boldsymbol{x})\right)}=1+o\left(f(\boldsymbol{x})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By this, we complete the proof of (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of the error formula (<a href="#S5.E28" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is by setting the linear approximations (<a href="#S5.E25" title="In 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>)-(<a href="#S5.E26" title="In 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and the optimal constants for small regions (<a href="#S5.E27" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) in the error formula (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A6.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left(\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)-\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left(\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)-\left({\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathbf{x}},1}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathbf{x}},1}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(\boldsymbol{x})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{\beta,1}(\boldsymbol{x})+o\left(V(A_{i})^{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathbf{x}},1}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)+R_{p_{\mathbf{x}},1}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E97.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left({o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left({p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})+\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E98.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\left.+\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left({\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\left.+\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\left({\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}\right)\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The detailed proof of the equality (<a href="#A6.E97" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">97</span></a>) is lengthy and therefore omitted here; yet, the proof is based on little-o expressions for various integrals over products of little-o terms and moment of inertia, which are technically similar to other parts of the proof that are explicitly shown in this appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To continue to proof, we use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality to get</p>
<table id="A6.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E99.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\leq\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right)^{2}\leq\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E100.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\leq\left\lvert\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right\rvert\leq\left\|{{\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\leq\left\lvert\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})^{T}\left(\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)\right\rvert\leq\left\|{{\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we can upper bound (<a href="#A6.E98" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">98</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A6.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)\leq\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)\leq\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\left.+\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|{{\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{3}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\left.+\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|{{\nabla p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{3}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">The definition of the normalized second-moment of inertia (<a href="#S5.E24" title="In 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) implies that</p>
<table id="A6.E102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}=M(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}=M(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Using the definition of the normalized <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\sf th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>𝗍𝗁</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\sf th}</annotation></semantics></math> moment of inertia (<a href="#A6.E88" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">88</span></a>), for <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A6.E103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{3}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}=M_{3}(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{3}{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{3}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}=M_{3}(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{3}{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{3}{d}}\in o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{3}{d}}\in o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(A_{i})\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(A_{i})\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A6.E104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{3}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\in o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left\|{{\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{i}}}\right\|_{2}^{3}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\in o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p">Setting (<a href="#A6.E102" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">102</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E104" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>) in (<a href="#A6.Ex28" title="In F.1 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Constants and Test Error in Sum Form using Locally-Linear Approximations for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">101</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A6.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}M(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(o\left(V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}M(A_{i})\cdot d\cdot V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+d\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}M(A_{i})V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+o\left(V_{\sf max}^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+d\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}M(A_{i})V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)+o\left(V_{\sf max}^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\sf max}=\underset{i\in\{1,\dots,m\}}{\max}V(A_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\sf max}=\underset{i\in\{1,\dots,m\}}{\max}V(A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This concludes the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Additional Details on Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Corollary 5. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from the test error formula (<a href="#S5.E28" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), we omit the explicit inaccuracy term <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left(V_{\sf max}^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left(V_{\sf max}^{1+\frac{2}{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and develop as follows:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\leq\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mi>𝖻𝗈𝗎𝗇𝖽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\leq\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E107.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+d\sum_{i=1}^{m}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}M(A_{i})V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+d\sum_{i=1}^{m}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}M(A_{i})V(A_{i})^{1+\frac{2}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+d\sum_{i=1}^{m}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\mu(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\frac{1}{m^{2/d}\lambda^{2/d}\left(\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}V(A_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+d\sum_{i=1}^{m}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\mu(\boldsymbol{x}_{i})\frac{1}{m^{2/d}\lambda^{2/d}\left(\boldsymbol{x}_{i}\right)}V(A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d}{m^{2/d}}\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\frac{\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mu(\boldsymbol{x})}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d}{m^{2/d}}\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\frac{\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mu(\boldsymbol{x})}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mi>𝖻𝗈𝗎𝗇𝖽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth moment of inertia profile from Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
The developments in (<a href="#A6.E107" title="In F.2 Additional Details on Corollary ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">107</span></a>) use Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>-<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ 5 Approximation Error of MoE for Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and approximation of the sum as integral due to the small region assumption.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem 13. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>: The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error in the Multidimensional Case</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us develop a lower bound for the integral <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\frac{\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}{\frac{\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the test error upper bound formula of Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Corollary 12. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. This will lead to the segment density that minimizes the test error upper bound. By Hölder’s inequality,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\frac{1}{\lambda^{\frac{2}{d+2}}(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{d}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\lambda^{\frac{2}{d+2}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{2}{d+2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\frac{1}{\lambda^{\frac{2}{d+2}}(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{d}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\lambda^{\frac{2}{d+2}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{2}{d+2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\geq\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="22.278em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\geq\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the left side can be simplified, thus,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{2}{d+2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{2}{d+2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\quad\geq\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="13.278em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\quad\geq\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The density <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> integrates to 1, i.e., <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence, we get that</p>
<table id="A6.E110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}\geq\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{d}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}\geq\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the left side is the integral from the test error bound formulated in Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Corollary 12. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Hölder’s inequality in (<a href="#A6.Ex33" title="In F.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error in the Multidimensional Case ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">108</span></a>) is attained with equality if <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is linearly proportional to <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Namely, for a constant <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})=\zeta\cdot\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda(\boldsymbol{x})=\zeta\cdot\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\lambda^{2/d}(\boldsymbol{x})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which, using integration over <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and that the density integrates to 1, implies that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta=\frac{1}{\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{d}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta=\frac{1}{\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{\frac{d+2}{d}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the density that minimizes the integral in the left side of (<a href="#A6.E110" title="In F.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error in the Multidimensional Case ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">110</span></a>) is</p>
<table id="A6.E113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\sf UBM}(\boldsymbol{x})=\frac{\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}}{\int_{\boldsymbol{\xi}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{\xi})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{\xi})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{\xi}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝖴𝖡𝖬</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝝃</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝝃</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\sf UBM}(\boldsymbol{x})=\frac{\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}}{\int_{\boldsymbol{\xi}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{\xi})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{\xi})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{\xi}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The optimal density <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\sf UBM}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝖴𝖡𝖬</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\sf UBM}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> makes (<a href="#A6.E110" title="In F.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error in the Multidimensional Case ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">110</span></a>) to hold with equality. Then, plugging the right side of (<a href="#A6.E110" title="In F.3 Proof of Theorem : The Optimal Expert Segment Density and the Corresponding Test Error in the Multidimensional Case ‣ Appendix F Proofs for the Case of Multidimensional Inputs ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">110</span></a>) into the the test error bound formulated in Corollary <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Corollary 12. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> gives the minimal bound of</p>
<table id="A6.E114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound,min}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d\cdot M(A_{d}^{\sf opt})}{m^{2/d}}\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{1+\frac{2}{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi><mrow><mi>𝖻𝗈𝗎𝗇𝖽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{E}}_{\sf test}^{\sf bound,min}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\frac{d\cdot M(A_{d}^{\sf opt})}{m^{2/d}}\left({\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in[0,1]^{d}}\left({\left\|{{\nabla\beta(\boldsymbol{x})}}\right\|_{2}^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})}\right)^{\frac{d}{d+2}}\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}\right)^{1+\frac{2}{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Theorem 13. ‣ Appendix C MoE for Multidimensional Inputs: The Expert Segment Density that Minimizes the Test-Error Upper Bound ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Proofs for Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>: The Learned Constant Expert is Unbiased</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the learned constant formula in (<a href="#S6.E35" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), the formula for expectation conditioned on an event (here the event is <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), the conditional expectation rule, the independence among <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for a specific region <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the definition (<a href="#S6.E34" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) of <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as the sum of all the variables <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}&gt;0}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}&gt;0}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}\cdot\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}=\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]\cdot\frac{1}{n_{i}}\sum_{j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1}y^{({j})}}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}\cdot\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}=\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]\cdot\frac{1}{n_{i}}\sum_{j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1}y^{({j})}}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]\cdot\frac{1}{n_{i}}\sum_{j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1}\mathbb{E}\left[{{y^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}=1}}\right]}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]\cdot\frac{1}{n_{i}}\sum_{j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1}\mathbb{E}\left[{{y^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}=1}}\right]}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the value of <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({j})}</annotation></semantics></math> is 1 in the conditional expectation of <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{({j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{({j})}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sum due the condition <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1</annotation></semantics></math> in the summation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the training data model (<a href="#S6.E32" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) and the zero mean of the noise, the inner conditional expectation in (<a href="#A7.E115" title="In G.1 Proof of Theorem : The Learned Constant Expert is Unbiased ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">115</span></a>) can be developed as follows:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{y^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)+\epsilon^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[{{\epsilon^{({j})}}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{y^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)+\epsilon^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[{{\epsilon^{({j})}}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)|q_{i}^{({j})}}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({j})}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Bernoulli random variable with</p>
<table id="A7.E117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E117.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Prob\left[{q_{i}^{({j})}=1}\right]=\Prob\left[{\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\in A_{i}}\right]=\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{q_{i}^{({j})}=1}\right]=\Prob\left[{\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\in A_{i}}\right]=\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Then, the expectation of <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{({j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{({j})}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the event <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({j})}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({j})}=1</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A7.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{y^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}=1}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)|q_{i}^{({j})}=1}}\right]=\frac{\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}{\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}=c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{y^{({j})}|q_{i}^{({j})}=1}}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[{{\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}^{({j})}\right)|q_{i}^{({j})}=1}}\right]=\frac{\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}\beta\left(\boldsymbol{x}\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}{\int_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}=c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where the last equality is due to the formula of the optimal constant (without small region assumptions) from (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Setting (<a href="#A7.E118" title="In G.1 Proof of Theorem : The Learned Constant Expert is Unbiased ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">118</span></a>) back in (<a href="#A7.E115" title="In G.1 Proof of Theorem : The Learned Constant Expert is Unbiased ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">115</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A7.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}&gt;0}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}&gt;0}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E119.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]\cdot\frac{1}{n_{i}}\cdot n_{i}c_{i}^{\sf opt}}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]\cdot\frac{1}{n_{i}}\cdot n_{i}c_{i}^{\sf opt}}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\left\{q_{i}^{({j})}\right\}_{j=1}^{n}}\left[{{\mathbb{I}[n_{i}&gt;0]}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1\cdot\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}c_{i}^{\sf opt}=c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1\cdot\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;0}\right]}c_{i}^{\sf opt}=c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We develop the test error for the learned expert constants, starting from the test error formula of (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A7.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{\widetilde{c}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{\widetilde{c}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}+c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}+c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E120.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+2\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+2\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">According to (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), the second sum in (<a href="#A7.E120" title="In G.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">120</span></a>) is related to test error of MoE with optimal constant experts (for a given routing segmentation) as</p>
<table id="A7.E121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}=\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)-\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)^{2}p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}=\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)-\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, for the third sum in (<a href="#A7.E120" title="In G.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">120</span></a>), note that</p>
<table id="A7.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\left(c_{i}^{\sf opt}-\beta(\boldsymbol{x})\right)p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{i}^{\sf opt}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}-\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{i}^{\sf opt}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}-\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}\cdot\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}-\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}{\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}\cdot\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}-\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\beta(\boldsymbol{x})p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the optimal constant formula (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) is used here.
Setting (<a href="#A7.E121" title="In G.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">121</span></a>) and (<a href="#A7.E122" title="In G.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">122</span></a>) back in (<a href="#A7.E120" title="In G.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">120</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A7.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{\widetilde{c}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{\widetilde{c}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)+\sum_{i=1}^{m}{\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Using that, by (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A7.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\sf app}\left(\mathcal{H}_{m,d}^{c}\left(\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\right)\right)=\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝖺𝗉𝗉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝗍𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\sf app}\left(\mathcal{H}_{m,d}^{c}\left(\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\right)\right)=\mathcal{E}_{\sf test}\left({\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m},\left\{c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\}_{i=1}^{m}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">and defining the estimation error, using <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho_{i}=\Prob\left[{\mathbf{x}\in A_{i}}\right]=\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=\Prob\left[{\mathbf{x}\in A_{i}}\right]=\int\displaylimits_{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{p_{\mathbf{x}}(\boldsymbol{x})\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S6.E36" title="In 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), as</p>
<table id="A7.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\sf est}(m,\mathcal{S}_{n})=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\rho_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\sf est}(m,\mathcal{S}_{n})=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">completes the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The definition of <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({j})}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S6.E33" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) implies it is a Bernoulli random variable with probability <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall (<a href="#S6.E36" title="In 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>)) of <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({j})}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({j})}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, definition (<a href="#S6.E34" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) implies that <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> independent Bernoulli variables <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({1})},\dots,q_{i}^{({n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({1})},\dots,q_{i}^{({n})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A version of the Chernoff bound for a sum of independent Bernoulli variables <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vershynin, 2018</a>)</cite> can be written here as</p>
<table id="A7.E124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E124.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{for}~\tau\in(0,1),~\Prob\left[{n_{i}\leq(1-\tau)\mathbb{E}\left[{{n_{i}}}\right]}\right]\leq\exp{\left(-\frac{\tau^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{{n_{i}}}\right]}{2}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>for</mtext><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{for}~\tau\in(0,1),~\Prob\left[{n_{i}\leq(1-\tau)\mathbb{E}\left[{{n_{i}}}\right]}\right]\leq\exp{\left(-\frac{\tau^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{{n_{i}}}\right]}{2}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">According to (<a href="#S6.E33" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), (<a href="#S6.E34" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), (<a href="#S6.E36" title="In 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A7.E125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{{n_{i}}}\right]=n\rho_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{{n_{i}}}\right]=n\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and therefore (<a href="#A7.E124" title="In G.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">124</span></a>) becomes</p>
<table id="A7.E126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E126.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{for}~\tau\in(0,1),~\Prob\left[{n_{i}\leq(1-\tau)n\rho_{i}}\right]\leq\exp{\left(-\frac{\tau^{2}n\rho_{i}}{2}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>for</mtext><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{for}~\tau\in(0,1),~\Prob\left[{n_{i}\leq(1-\tau)n\rho_{i}}\right]\leq\exp{\left(-\frac{\tau^{2}n\rho_{i}}{2}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Upper bounding the right-side probability in (<a href="#A7.E126" title="In G.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">126</span></a>) with <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> yields the condition</p>
<table id="A7.E127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\frac{2}{\tau^{2}\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\frac{2}{\tau^{2}\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Then, setting <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A7.E126" title="In G.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">126</span></a>) and (<a href="#A7.E127" title="In G.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">127</span></a>) gives that for <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\frac{8}{\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\frac{8}{\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A7.E128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E128.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Prob\left[{n_{i}\leq\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}}\right]\leq\widetilde{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{n_{i}\leq\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}}\right]\leq\widetilde{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(128)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">The inequality in (<a href="#A7.E128" title="In G.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">128</span></a>) is equivalent to <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}}\right]\geq 1-\widetilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{n_{i}&gt;\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}}\right]\geq 1-\widetilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> is completed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">According to (<a href="#S6.E35" title="In 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{c}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{c}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an average of <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> independent random variables <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{y^{({j})}\right\}_{j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{y^{({j})}\right\}_{j:q_{i}^{({j})}=1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, conditioned on <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}=\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}=\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-random value, the probability distribution of the random variable <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{c}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{c}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as the probability distribution of the random variable</p>
<table id="A7.E129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\theta_{i}}\sum_{\tau=1}^{\theta_{i}}z_{i}^{(\tau)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\theta_{i}}\sum_{\tau=1}^{\theta_{i}}z_{i}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}^{(1)},\dots,z_{i}^{(\theta_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}^{(1)},\dots,z_{i}^{(\theta_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. drawn from the distribution of <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y|\{q_{i}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y|\{q_{i}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},y)</annotation></semantics></math> are drawn from the distribution of the data model (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{i}=\mathbb{I}[\mathbf{x}\in A_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\mathbb{I}[\mathbf{x}\in A_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We use the following assumptions in addition to the data model (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3 Problem and Model Definition ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):
The function <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded on its entire domain. For the <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\sf th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗍𝗁</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\sf th}</annotation></semantics></math> region <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote the value range size as <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta,i}\triangleq\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\max}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})-\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\min}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta,i}\triangleq\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\max}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})-\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\min}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The noise <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is from the bounded range <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\epsilon_{\sf min},\epsilon_{\sf max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\epsilon_{\sf min},\epsilon_{\sf max}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\epsilon}\triangleq\epsilon_{\sf max}-\epsilon_{\sf min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\epsilon}\triangleq\epsilon_{\sf max}-\epsilon_{\sf min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{({j})}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{({j})}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the random variable <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{({j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{({j})}</annotation></semantics></math> gets its value from the range</p>
<table id="A7.E130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\min}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf min},~\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\max}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf max}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\min}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf min},~\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\max}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf max}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(130)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The random variables <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}^{(1)},\dots,z_{i}^{(\theta_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}^{(1)},\dots,z_{i}^{(\theta_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math> are also from the value range (<a href="#A7.E130" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">130</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, for <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}=\theta_{i}}}\right]\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}=\theta_{i}}}\right]\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\frac{1}{\theta_{i}}\sum_{\tau=1}^{\theta_{i}}z_{i}^{(\tau)}-\frac{1}{\theta_{i}}\mathbb{E}\left[{{\sum_{\tau=1}^{\theta_{i}}z_{i}^{(\tau)}}}\right]\right\rvert\geq\gamma}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\frac{1}{\theta_{i}}\sum_{\tau=1}^{\theta_{i}}z_{i}^{(\tau)}-\frac{1}{\theta_{i}}\mathbb{E}\left[{{\sum_{\tau=1}^{\theta_{i}}z_{i}^{(\tau)}}}\right]\right\rvert\geq\gamma}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\theta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\theta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(131)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality is due to Hoeffding’s inequality; by (<a href="#A7.E130" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">130</span></a>), <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{{\sf max},i}=\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\max}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{{\sf max},i}=\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\max}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{{\sf min},i}=\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\min}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{{\sf min},i}=\underset{\boldsymbol{x}\in A_{i}}{\min}\beta(\boldsymbol{x})+\epsilon_{\sf min}</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore,</p>
<table id="A7.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}=R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}=R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(132)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that, according to Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 6.1 Learning Expert Constants via Least Squares ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, <math id="A7.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}&gt;0}}\right]=c_{i}^{\sf opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}&gt;0}}\right]=c_{i}^{\sf opt}</annotation></semantics></math>. It can be proved similarly to Appendix <a href="#A7.SS1" title="G.1 Proof of Theorem : The Learned Constant Expert is Unbiased ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> that</p>
<table id="A7.E133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}=\theta_{i}}}\right]=c_{i}^{\sf opt},~~\text{for}~\theta_{i}\in\{1,\dots,n\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{{\widetilde{c}_{i}|n_{i}=\theta_{i}}}\right]=c_{i}^{\sf opt},~~\text{for}~\theta_{i}\in\{1,\dots,n\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(133)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Then, setting (<a href="#A7.E133" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">133</span></a>) in (<a href="#A7.Ex45" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">131</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A7.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\theta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\theta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(134)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let us extend the conditioning such that <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\in\{\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\in\{\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive non-random value from the continuous range <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,n]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E135.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma,~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma,~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(135)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mo>|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msup><mo>|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em">]</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(136)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E137.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\theta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\theta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(137)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(138)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E139.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}{\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(139)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(140)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where the bound in (<a href="#A7.E137" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">137</span></a>) is due to (<a href="#A7.E134" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">134</span></a>), and (<a href="#A7.E139" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">139</span></a>) is due to<math id="A7.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]=\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]=\sum_{\theta_{i}=\left\lceil\eta_{i}\right\rceil}^{n}\Prob\left[{n_{i}=\theta_{i}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>; also, <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> due to the assumption that <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, we got</p>
<table id="A7.E141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>𝗆𝗂𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma~|~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2\gamma^{2}\eta_{i}}{\left(v_{{\sf max},i}-v_{{\sf min},i}\right)^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(141)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">The concentration inequality (<a href="#A7.E141" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">141</span></a>) can be equivalently written as follows. For <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}\in(0,n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}\in(0,n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.E142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{2\eta_{i}}}~\Bigg|~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Prob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Prob\left[{\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert\geq\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{2\eta_{i}}}~\Bigg|~n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}}\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(142)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Put differently, for <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}\in(0,n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}\in(0,n]</annotation></semantics></math>, and given <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\geq\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.E143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert&lt;\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{2\eta_{i}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert&lt;\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{2\eta_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(143)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.5" class="ltx_p">with probability at least <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that this theorem assumes <math id="A7.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, for <math id="A7.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and given <math id="A7.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\frac{8}{\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\frac{8}{\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}&gt;\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}&gt;\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A7.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\widetilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\widetilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, the probabilistic intersection of (<a href="#A7.E143" title="In G.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">143</span></a>) for <math id="A7.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}=\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}=\frac{1}{2}n\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> gives that for <math id="A7.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and given <math id="A7.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\frac{8}{\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\frac{8}{\rho_{i}}\ln{\left(\frac{1}{\widetilde{\delta}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.E144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert&lt;\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{n\rho_{i}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert&lt;\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{n\rho_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(144)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">with probability at least <math id="A7.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)-\widetilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)-\widetilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This completes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem11" title="Theorem 11. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof starts from the estimation error formula (<a href="#S6.E39" title="In Lemma 8. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and setting into it the upper bound of <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math> from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf est}(m,\mathcal{S}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝖾𝗌𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\sf est}(m,\mathcal{S}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E145.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right)^{2}\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(145)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E146.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{n\rho_{i}}}\right)^{2}\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\gamma\frac{R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}}{\sqrt{n\rho_{i}}}\right)^{2}\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(146)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma^{2}}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma^{2}}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\gamma^{2}}{n}m\cdot\underset{i\in\{1,\dots,m\}}{\max}\left(R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\gamma^{2}}{n}m\cdot\underset{i\in\{1,\dots,m\}}{\max}\left(R_{\beta,i}+R_{\epsilon}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The inequality in (<a href="#A7.E146" title="In G.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix G Proofs for Section ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">146</span></a>) is due to applying Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> to upper bound <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math> each of the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> experts in the sum. These <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> applications of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem 10. ‣ 6.2 Test Error Analysis for MoE with Learned Expert Constants ‣ 6 Learning the Constant Experts: A Tradeoff in the Number of Experts ‣ Mixture of Many Zero-Compute Experts:A High-Rate Quantization Theory Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> are for the same <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\delta}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For each of the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> experts, the upper bound for <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>𝗈𝗉𝗍</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert\widetilde{c}_{i}-c_{i}^{\sf opt}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math> holds with probability at least <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)-\widetilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)-\widetilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence, the upper bounds hold for all the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> experts with probability at least <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2m\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)-m\widetilde{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2m\exp\left(-\gamma^{2}\right)-m\widetilde{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
